# Wave W17-V (Route 205): hive box — a hive-yard box standing in the flower grass beside the shipped honeytree: a stacked wooden hive with two pale hive bands and the dark round flight hole, bees implied by the yard, not drawn (design: dripping hive yards in the flower grass under the honey trees). On gale turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by form entire: this prop is furniture, not signage; the valley keeps its honey in boxes.
